Tigris_FSScan_SkipTypes names file system types the file system scan
should leave out, but this run could not apply it, and scanned those
file systems with the rest.

Auditing a system that is not running (tigris --root), the file systems
under the root are the ones this host mounted there: an image unpacked
on a ZFS dataset is not a system that keeps its files on ZFS, and the
audited system's own mount table is not there to read. On a system
whose find has no -xdev, or which has no gen_mounts, the scan walks /
as one tree and never learns where one file system ends.

Tigris_FSScan_SkipMounts works in both cases: it names the mount points
by their paths on the audited system, and the scan does not walk those
directories (con021c says which). Tigris_FSScan_PruneDirs leaves out
any directory by a pattern.
